Theorem TF-2: Transfer function signatures — forward TF + backward backwardDemand + TF-13 + TF-14

  Preconditions:
    - Forward transfer function definitions per Annex E §AIMS
      operate on AimsState x Instr -> AimsState
    - Backward demand definitions per Annex E §AIMS (TF-11, TF-11a)
      operate on ArcInstr -> List <ArcVarId, Cardinality, Consumption>
    - TF-13 capture_state_update is the closure-capture transfer
      per Annex E §AIMS TF-13 (OxCaml LAM pattern)
    - TF-14 propagate_project_source_demand is the Project backward-demand
      propagation per Annex E §AIMS.9 + TF-14
    - Per-Instr forward definitions (TF-1 through TF-15a) and per-Instr
      backward-demand patterns (TF-11, TF-11a, TF-12, TF-13, TF-14)
      discharged at sec-04; sec-01 authors signatures + skeletons only

  Soundness property:
    Forward transfer signature (per the canonical proof notation:198):

      TF : AimsState -> Instr -> AimsState

      Per-instruction definitions (Appendix A canonical Forward Transfer Matrix):
        TF-1 Let Literal -> SCALAR (all dimensions)
        TF-2 Let Var(v) -> state(v)
        TF-2a Let PrimOp -> SCALAR
        TF-3 Construct(ctor) -> FRESH(shape_from_ctor(ctor))
        TF-4 Project(value, field) -> (B, L, 1, src.uniq, src.loc, Phi, NONE)
                                          + borrow_sources entry
        TF-5 Apply (no contract) -> CONSERVATIVE
        TF-5a ApplyIndirect -> CONSERVATIVE
        TF-6 Apply (contract) -> refine(CONSERVATIVE, callee.return_contract)
        TF-6a Invoke (contract) -> same as TF-6
        TF-6b Invoke (no contract) -> CONSERVATIVE
        TF-6c InvokeIndirect -> CONSERVATIVE
        TF-7 PartialApply -> FRESH(Phi); captures via TF-13
        TF-8 Select -> scalar-exclusion join
        TF-9 Reuse -> FRESH(inherited shape)
        TF-9a CollectionReuse -> FRESH(C)
        TF-10 IsShared -> SCALAR
        TF-10a Reset -> SCALAR
        TF-15 Set -> no dst; IA-5 step (1) handles value
        TF-15a SetTag -> no dst; only base receives demand

    Backward demand signature (per the canonical proof notation:212 +
    Annex E §AIMS TF-11 + TF-11a):

      backwardDemand : ArcInstr -> List <ArcVarId, Cardinality, Consumption>

      Per-instruction backward-demand patterns:
        TF-11 standard <operand, 1, L> with seq_add accumulation across
                multiple instructions defining demand on same variable
        TF-11a terminator demands per Annex E §AIMS TF-11a table
                (Return, Jump, Branch, Switch, Invoke, InvokeIndirect,
                 Resume, Unreachable)
        TF-12 PartialApply emits NO TF-11 demand; captures handled by TF-13
        TF-13 capture_state_update transfers closure-context state to
                captured variables per OxCaml LAM (closure cardinality
                Once: consumption seq_add Affine + locality max;
                cardinality > Once: Unrestricted + Many + max)
        TF-14 propagate_project_source_demand widens
                src.cardinality seq_add dst.cardinality +
                src.locality max dst.locality +
                src.consumption seq_add Affine

      seq_add Consumption matrix per Annex E §AIMS TF-11:
        Dead + X = X
        Linear + Linear = Unrestricted
        Linear + Affine = Unrestricted
        Affine + Affine = Unrestricted
        X + Unrestricted = Unrestricted

    TF-13 signature:

      capture_state_update : AimsState x AimsState -> AimsState
      capture_state_update(current, closure_state) = new_state

    TF-14 signature:

      propagate_project_source_demand : AimsStateMap x ArcVarId -> AimsStateMap

